In terms of how quicksort works, it is a divide and conquer algorithm. It works by selecting a 'pivot' element from the array and partitioning the other elements into two sub-arrays, according to whether they are less than or greater than the pivot. After this partitioning, the pivot is in its final position. This is called the partition operation. Quicksort then recursively applies this process to the sub-arrays. The recursion ends when the array has just one element, as it is sorted by definition then.

