a:
I believe there may be some confusion as the problem seems to ask for a solution in Python but the given example is in C++.
The given problem cannot be solved using C++ as requested because by design, Python and C++ handle string mutations differently (Python strings are immutable whereas C++ strings are mutable). 

If you desire a C++ solution, here it is:

```cpp
#include<iostream>
#include<string>

std::string reverse_string(std::string str) {
  int l = 0;
  int r = str.length() - 1;

  while(l < r){
    if(!isalpha(str[l])){
      l++;
    }else if(!isalpha(str[r])){
      r--;
    }else {
      std::swap(str[l], str[r]);
      str[l] = toupper(str[l]);
      str[r] = toupper(str[r]);
      l++;
      r--;
    }
  }
  return str;
}
```

