Implement a C++ program that finds the intersection of two distinct integer arrays. An intersection means that these are common elements present in both arrays. The first one-dimensional integer array named arr1[] contains seven numbers: [12, 4, 17, 6, 21, 45, 33]. The second one-dimensional integer array named arr2[] holds five values: [9, 21, 47, 33, 4]. Use standard algorithms present in the STL library to achieve this. 

Here is a preliminary piece of code that attempts to solve the problem but contains one or more errors. Note that this is a flawed implementation, and it is up to you to debug, correct and optimize the code:

```C++
