#include<vector>
#include<unordered_set>

bool hasPairWithSum8(const std::vector<int>& array) {
    std::unordered_set<int> seen;
    for (int num : array) {
        if (seen.find(8 - num) != seen.end())
            return true;
        seen.insert(num);
    }
    return false;
}
``` 

This function works in O(n) time where n is the size of the input array. It will stop and return true as soon as it finds a pair of numbers that sum to 8, so in the best case scenario it could return in constant time if the first two numbers sum to 8. If no such pair exists, it will spend constant time checking each element of the array once, hence the O(n) time complexity.

