- If the node to be deleted has one child, update the parent of the node to be deleted to point to the child of the node to be deleted.
- If the node to be deleted has two children, find the in-order successor of the node (the smallest node in the right subtree), copy its data to the node to be deleted, and then recursively delete the in-order successor node.

