    del->next = del->prev->next;
}
```

This line of code tries to bypass `del` by changing `del->next`, but the effect is immediately lost when `del` is deleted. Moreover, it should be assigning to `del->prev->next`, not `del->next`. The correct line should be:

```cpp
if (del->prev != NULL) {
    del->prev->next = del->next;
}
```

