    cout << "Array after removal: ";
    printArray(arr, n);

    return 0;
}
```

In this implementation, we pass by reference the size of the array `n` to the `removeSecondElement` function, because we need to update it in place as we are removing an element. After the removal, we decrement `n` to account for the new size of our array.

