This program creates a map of matching pairs of opening and closing brackets. It then iterates over the input string character by character, and if it finds an opening bracket, it pushes it onto the stack. If it finds a closing bracket, it checks if the stack is not empty, and if the top element of the stack matches the closing bracket it pops from the stack. If there's a mismatch, it returns false. If the stack is empty at the end of the string, it means all brackets have been matched properly, and it returns true.

