a:
The code to resolve the issue would be as follows. The main approach is to initialize two pointers pointing to the start and end of the string. Traverse the string till the two pointers meet and if both the characters at the pointers are alphabets, swap them, otherwise move the pointer(s).

We need to include '#include<algorithm>' for 'swap' and '#include<cctype>' for 'isalpha'. Here is the corrected code -

```C++
#include<iostream>
#include<string>
#include<algorithm>
#include<cctype>

std::string reverseString(std::string str) {
    int i = 0, j = str.length() - 1;

    while(i < j) {
        if(!isalpha(str[i])) {
            i++;
            continue;
        }
        if(!isalpha(str[j])) {
            j--;
            continue;
        }
        std::swap(str[i], str[j]);
        i++;
        j--;
    }
    return str;
}

int main() {
   std::cout << reverseString("#$@!abcd1234") << std::endl;
   std::cout << reverseString("*$&acd321@") << std::endl;
   return 0;
}
```
