	print_backward_recursion(p->next);  // Recursively call the function with the next node
	cout<<p->data<<" ";  // Print the data of the current node after the recursive call
}
```

The `print_backward_recursion` function uses recursion to traverse the linked list in reverse order. It first checks for the base case where the current node is NULL, indicating the end of the list. Then, it recursively calls itself with the next node and prints the data of the current node after the recursive call, effectively printing the linked list in reverse order.

