Write a C++ program to print all prime numbers in a range provided as input by the user. The user should be able to define both the lowest and the highest values of this range, and your code should check for erroneous cases such as negative numbers or non-integer characters. Make sure your prime-checking algorithm is as efficient as possible.

As a hint, here's a piece of code that tries to compute prime numbers. Identify the errors and use this as a reference when creating your own code.

```C++
