int treeDepth(Node* root) {
    if (root == nullptr) {
        return 0;
    } else {
        int leftDepth = treeDepth(root->left);
        int rightDepth = treeDepth(root->right);
        return 1 + std::max(leftDepth, rightDepth);
    }
}
```

The `treeDepth` function recursively calculates the depth of the binary tree. If the root is null, the depth is 0. Otherwise, it calculates the depth of the left and right subtrees and returns the maximum depth plus 1, representing the current level. This approach efficiently computes the depth of the binary tree in O(n) time, where n is the number of nodes in the tree.

