        return False
    lower_case = sum([k.islower() for k in dct.keys()])
    upper_case = sum([k.isupper() for k in dct.keys()])
    return lower_case == len(dct) or upper_case == len(dct)
I'd appreciate some explanation for the C++ version of the code.

a:
The original Python function is checking if all the keys in a dictionary are either entirely lowercase or entirely uppercase. We can achieve the same thing using a combination of C++ std::map (equivalent to Python's dict), for_each(), and lambdas.

Here is the equivalent C++ function:

```cpp
#include <map>
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>

bool check_dict_case(std::map<std::string, int>& dct) {
    if (dct.empty())
        return false;

    int lower_case = 0, upper_case = 0;

    std::for_each(dct.begin(), dct.end(), [&](const std::pair<std::string, int> &d) {
        std::string key = d.first;
        bool is_lower = std::all_of(key.begin(), key.end(), ::islower);
        bool is_upper = std::all_of(key.begin(), key.end(), ::isupper);

        if (is_lower) 
            ++lower_case;
        else if (is_upper) 
            ++upper_case;
    });

    return lower_case == dct.size() || upper_case == dct.size();
}
```

Firstly, `for_each()` accepts three arguments: begin and end iterators of the range we want to iterate and a function to apply to each element in this range. In our case, the range is our dictionary (map in C++), and the function is a lambda.

The lambda function `&[ ](const std::pair<…>{…}` captures all in surrounding by reference. Then the function runs for each `std::pair` contained in the dictionary - a pair consists of a key (string) and a value (integer).

Inside the lambda function, for each key (d.first), `all_of` checks if all characters are either lower or upper. `::islower` and `::isupper` are standard C++ functions checking if a given character is lower or upper case.

Whenever it finds all the characters in a key to be lower case or upper case, it increments the respective count.

Finally, outside the `for_each()`, the function checks if all keys in the dictionary are either entirely lower case or upper case by comparing the count to the size of the dictionary.

