#include <algorithm>

// checks if a string is a palindrome
bool is_palindrome(const std::string & str) 
{
    std::string cleaned; 
    for (char c : str) 
    {        
        if (isalnum(c)) 
        {
            cleaned += tolower(c);
        }
    }

    std::string reversed(cleaned);
    std::reverse(reversed.begin(), reversed.end());

    return cleaned == reversed;
}
```

Here we accomplish `cleaned = ''.join(c for c in string if c.isalnum()).lower()`, we create an empty string and append alphanumeric characters of provided string to it one by one after converting to lowercase using tolower(). Then we reverse it by creating a copy and compare the cleaned and reversed string.

