Below is one way to implement such a class in C++. This code creates a class called StringCharacterCounter that does what is described in the problem. It uses a map to store the counts and a queue to maintain the order. The GetFirstNonRepeatingCharacter() method simply dequeues elements until it finds a character with a count of 1.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <map>

class StringCharacterCounter {
private:
    std::map<char, int> counts;
    std::queue<char> order;

public:
    void AddCharacter(char c) {
        if (counts.find(c) != counts.end()) {
            counts[c]++;
        } else {
            counts.insert(std::make_pair(c, 1));
            order.push(c);
        }
    }

    char GetFirstNonRepeatingCharacter() {
        while (!order.empty() && counts[order.front()] > 1) {
            order.pop();
        }

        if (order.empty()) {
            throw std::runtime_error("No non-repeating characters found");
        }

        return order.front();
    }
};

int main() {
    StringCharacterCounter counter;

    counter.AddCharacter('a');
    counter.AddCharacter('b');
    counter.AddCharacter('c');
    counter.AddCharacter('a');
    counter.AddCharacter('b');
    counter.AddCharacter('c');
    counter.AddCharacter('d');

    std::cout << "First non-repeating character: " << counter.GetFirstNonRepeatingCharacter() << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This C++ code creates a class for counting occurrences of characters in a string, maintaining order, and finding the first non-repeating character. It is optimized for time complexity by using a map and queue data structure for efficient operations.

Please note that the AddCharacter(char c) function has time complexity O(1) as we are either inserting into the map or Incrementing the count in the map which are both O(1) operations and also pushing character into queue which is also O(1) operation. The GetFirstNonRepeatingCharacter() function has time complexity O(1) for average case as it only access the front of the queue and pops out the elements from queue. In worst case, it might have to pop out all the elements from queue, hence the worst case time complexity for GetFirstNonRepeatingCharacter() can be O(n).

