To solve the problem, we can use C++ OOP (Object Oriented Programming) to create a class called Tetrahedron. Since the surface area of a tetrahedron is sqrt(3) * side ^2, we'd need the side length as an instance variable.

However, n-dimensional tetrahedrons (specifically, 4-dimensional ones, also known as Simplexes) have a bit more complex calculation, so we can separate that into a different class for inheritence. The volume of n-dimensional tetrahedron requires factorial calculation, so we can also implement a factorial function.

Please note that any n-dimensional tetrahedron (n>3) does not make geometrical sense in our universe. Here is code skeleton.

```cpp
#include<iostream>
#include<cmath>
using namespace std;

class Tetrahedron {
protected:
    double side;
public:
    Tetrahedron(double side = 1){
        if(side <= 0){
            cout << "Invalid Input. Side length must be positive." << endl;
            exit(0);
        }
        this->side = side;
    }

    double surfaceArea(){
        return sqrt(3)*pow(side,2);
    }
};

class nDimensionalTetrahedron : public Tetrahedron{
public:
    nDimensionalTetrahedron(double side = 1) : Tetrahedron(side) {}

    double factorial(int num){
        if(num == 0 || num == 1) return 1;
        return num*factorial(num-1);
    }

    double volumeNdimension(int n){
        if(n <= 0){
            cout << "Dimension must be a positive integer" << endl;
            exit(0);
        }

        return pow(side,n) / (factorial(n) * pow(n,n/2));
    }
};

int main(){
    Tetrahedron t(5);
    cout << "Surface Area of Tetrahedron: " << t.surfaceArea() << endl;

    nDimensionalTetrahedron nt(5);
    cout << "Volume of 4-Dimensional Tetrahedron: " << nt.volumeNdimension(4) << endl;

    return 0;
}
```
The above code would calculate the volume of 4-dimensional tetrahedron. Note that there is no surface area for a 4-dimensional tetrahedron in our 3-dimensional space. But you can calculate its "hyper-volume" using the method `volumeNdimension`.

Please ensure to provide a valid positive number as side length. A zero or negative number as side length or dimension is invalid as per the error handling in the code.

