The given algorithm creates a dynamic 2D array in the heap memory, initializes the array, and leaves the memory allocated without freeing it which would inevitably lead to memory leaks. The problem lies in the inefficient use of memory allocation and deallocation. As the scope of the array is throughout the program, not deallocating the same would make this space unreachable leading to wastage of space or memory leak.

Here are some techniques to optimize memory usage :

1. Use a flat memory layout: A 2D array can be represented as a single array in which elements are carefully arranged. This reduces the array creation overhead.

2. Deallocation of Memory: Always deallocate the memory that has been allocated in heap by using the delete keyword in C++. This helps to prevent memory leaks. 

3. Use std::arrays or std::vector: these offer advantages such as static memory allocation or dynamic memory allocation as in the case of a vector. These containers also provide easier iterator-based methods to traverse the 2D array.

