        arr[i][j] = i*j;
    }
}
```

This version of the program uses a vector instead of raw arrays, which avoids manual memory management and gives you more convenient interfaces to work with. Furthermore, vectors are contiguous in memory, which is more cache friendly and can therefore offer better performance than linked structures. 

