- `n`: an integer representing the number of independent variables
- `m`: an integer representing the number of dependent variables
- `a1x`: a vector of size `n` containing the independent variables
- `a2x`: a vector of size `n` containing the independent variables at the second level
- `a2y`: a vector of size `m` containing the dependent variables at the second level

The function should perform higher-order automatic differentiation using the CppAD library and return the second-level derivatives of the dependent variables with respect to the independent variables.

