Develop a C++ program that accomplishes the following task:

Given an input string that contains composed of several groups of nested parentheses, the function should separate each nested parentheses group into individual strings and return them in a vector. Each group can have nested parentheses and may also have unequal distribution of parentheses in each nesting level. Ignore any whitespace in the input string.
>>> separate_nested_paren_groups("(( )) ((( )) (( )( )))")
{"(())", "((()))", "((()()))"}

