class IOReleaser {
public:
    IOReleaser(io_object_t obj) : toRelease(obj) {}
    ~IOReleaser() {
        if (toRelease != 0)
            IOObjectRelease(toRelease);
    }
    IOReleaser(IOReleaser&& moved) : toRelease(moved.toRelease) {
        moved.toRelease = 0;
    }
    IOReleaser(IOReleaser const&) = delete;

    // Move assignment operator
    IOReleaser& operator=(IOReleaser&& moved) {
        if (this != &moved) {
            if (toRelease != 0) {
                IOObjectRelease(toRelease);
            }
            toRelease = moved.toRelease;
            moved.toRelease = 0;
        }
        return *this;
    }

    // Move constructor
    IOReleaser(IOReleaser&& moved) : toRelease(moved.toRelease) {
        moved.toRelease = 0;
    }

    // Getter for the io_object_t
    io_object_t get() const {
        return toRelease;
    }

private:
    io_object_t toRelease;
};
```

In the solution, the missing member functions `operator=` and the move constructor are added to the `IOReleaser` class to support move semantics and proper resource management. The move assignment operator ensures that the resource is properly released before transferring ownership, and the move constructor transfers ownership of the resource while nullifying the moved object's resource. Additionally, a getter function `get` is provided to retrieve the `io_object_t` from the `IOReleaser` object.

