Why is there a memory leak?
The memory leak is happening because of unlimited dynamic allocation ('new LeakTest()') of memory in the infinite loop in the main function and there is no corresponding deallocation ('delete') for the allocated memory. This continues until all the memory available to the program is used up, that leads to memory leak. The destructor will not be called automatically when creating object dynamically using new, therefore each allocation gets piled up as a memory leak.

What would be the corrected code?
The correct version would include a 'delete' operation to deallocate the memory reserved by 'new'. The corrected code is given below:

