This C++ code sorts the array in descending order using the insertion sort algorithm. For each entry in the array, it finds the proper place to insert the value while keeping the array sorted in descending order.

Time complexity:
- Worst case: The worst-case scenario is O(n^2), which occurs when the array is sorted in ascending order.
- Best case: The best case scenario occurs when the array is already sorted in descending order, in this scenario the time complexity is O(n).

