Here is a C++ program to find the longest substring in a given string which contains all unique characters.

```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <map>

std::string longestUniqueSubstring(std::string str) {
    std::map<char, int> seen;
    unsigned long start = 0, maxLen = 0;
    std::string maxStr = "";

    for (unsigned long i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
        if (seen.find(str[i]) != seen.end()) {
            start = std::max(start, seen[str[i]] + 1);
        }

        if (i - start + 1 > maxLen) {
            maxLen = i - start + 1;
            maxStr = str.substr(start, maxLen);
        }

        seen[str[i]] = i;
    }

    return maxStr;
}

int main() {
    std::string input = "abcdefghigklmnopqrstuvwxyz";
    std::string res = longestUniqueSubstring(input);
    std::cout << "The longest unique character substring is: " << res << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This program uses a two pointer sliding window approach. It starts from the beginning of the string and uses a map to store the most recent index of each character. The 'start' variable gets updated whenever a repeating character is found. Meanwhile, the current longest unique substring is constantly updating if the current substring is longer. The 'maxLen' variable keeps track of the length of the longest unique substring, and 'maxStr' is used to hold the longest unique substring.

So the first time it sees a repeating character, it moves the start to the next character of the first repeating one and continues parsing. The algorithm does this because the characters before the first repeating one might be part of other unique substrings that start at a character after 'start'. If the substring from 'start' to 'i' (both inclusive) contains all unique characters, it has a chance to be the longest unique substring. It then compares its length with the length of previous longest unique substring (if any), and if it is longer, then updates the longest unique substring.

When the end of the string is reached, the longest unique substring found is returned.

