Write a multi-threaded C++ program that generates Fibonacci numbers up to a maximum of n values and also identifies and corrects potential race conditions or other concurrency issues. The program output should have thread-safe display, meaning that the printing of the fibonacci sequence should always maintain the correct order. As a reference, consider the code provided which exhibits a race condition. Identify the issue and correct it in your program implementation.

