In order to solve this problem, we need to generate a list of all prime numbers less than or equal to the given number using the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm. Afterwards, we use 3 nested loops (brute force) to generate all possible combinations of 3 numbers and count those combinations where these 3 numbers add up to the given number.

