    explicit Query(const std::string& str) {
        parse(str);
    }

    void parse(const std::string& str) {
        // split the string and store the parts in the vector
    }

    // You can then provide whatever methods you want to access the parts.
};
```

This gives you full control over your public API, and does not expose any methods from std::vector that you do not want to expose.

