Here is the C++ version:

```cpp
#include <algorithm>
#include <string>
#include <cctype>

bool is_palindrome(const std::string& str) {
    std::string sanitize_string;

    for (char c : str)
        if (std::isalnum(c))
            sanitize_string += std::tolower(c);

    int strlen = sanitize_string.length();
    if (strlen == 0 || strlen == 1)
        return true;

    if (sanitize_string[0] != sanitize_string[strlen - 1])
        return false;

    return is_palindrome(sanitize_string.substr(1, strlen - 2));
}

std::string make_palindrome_recursive(const std::string& orig_string, std::string sanitize_string) {
    if (is_palindrome(sanitize_string)) {
        std::string reversed_orig_string = orig_string;
        std::reverse(reversed_orig_string.begin(), reversed_orig_string.end());
        return orig_string + reversed_orig_string.substr(orig_string.length() - sanitize_string.length());
    }
    else {
        return make_palindrome_recursive(orig_string, sanitize_string.substr(0, sanitize_string.length() - 1));
    }
}

std::string make_palindrome(const std::string& str) {
    std::string sanitize_string;

    for (char c : str)
        if (std::isalnum(c))
            sanitize_string += std::tolower(c);

    int strlen = sanitize_string.length();
    if (strlen == 0)
        return "";

    if (strlen == 1)
        return str;

    if (is_palindrome(sanitize_string))
        return str;

    return make_palindrome_recursive(str, sanitize_string);
}
```

In the `is_palindrome()` function, we sanitize the input string by stripping it of non-alphanumeric characters and converting it to lowercase. If the resulting string is empty or contains only one character, it is a palindrome by definition. If the first and last characters of the string do not match, the string is not a palindrome. Otherwise, we recurse down to a smaller string by removing the first and last characters.

In the `make_palindrome_recursive()` function, we check if the sanitized string is a palindrome. If it is, we construct a palindrome from the original string by concatenating it with its reverse, omitting the part of the reversed string that matches the palindrome. If the sanitized string is not a palindrome, we shorten it by one character and recurse.

In the `make_palindrome()` function, we sanitize the input string, check for special cases (an empty string and a single-character string), and return the original string if it is already a palindrome. Otherwise, we call `make_palindrome_recursive()`.

