Please remember that the division operation (/) and modulus operation (%) (checking for non-remainder results, `n%i==0`) are essential part of the program. The `for` loop operates from `2` to `sqrt(n)` because all possible divisors of a number `n` can be found within this range. If `n` is divisible by `i` (hence `n%i==0`), then `i` and `n/i` are divisors of `n`. If `i` equals `n/i` (when `n` is a perfect square), we add `i` only once to prevent duplication.

