We use `pow` function to calculate the square of the difference of coordinates, and `sqrt` function to compute the square root of the sum of these squares which gives us the Euclidean distance between the two points.

We also include a check for case when both points are identical by checking if the difference in all coordinates is zero. If it is, we print an appropriate message and return `0` as the distance.

